#: src/project/bindings/java.md:1
msgid "prql-java"
msgstr ""

#: src/project/bindings/java.md:3
msgid ""
"`prql-java` offers Java bindings to the `prqlc` Rust library, through [JNI]"
"(https://docs.oracle.com/javase/8/docs/technotes/guides/jni/). It exposes "
"three native methods on `org.prql.prql4j.PrqlCompiler`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/project/bindings/java.md:13
msgid ""
"`target` is a dialect name such as `sql.mysql` — see [Target and version]"
"(https://prql-lang.org/book/project/target.html) for the full list. `format` "
"controls whether the SQL is pretty-printed, and `signature` whether the "
"trailing `-- Generated by PRQL compiler version:...` comment is included."
msgstr ""

#: src/project/bindings/java.md:19
msgid ""
"It's still at an early stage, and currently requires compiling locally, and "
"isn't published to Maven. Contributions are welcome."
msgstr ""

#: src/project/bindings/java.md:22
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: src/project/bindings/java.md:24
msgid ""
"Build the bindings and install them into your local Maven repository from "
"`java/`. The jar this produces does not bundle the native library — only the "
"`deploy` profile's `cross.sh` step populates `src/main/resources` — so "
"consumers need `libprql_java` from the workspace's `target/release` on `java."
"library.path`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/project/bindings/java.md:31
msgid ""
"# `-Dgpg.skip=true` because `java/pom.xml` binds `maven-gpg-plugin` to the\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/project/bindings/java.md:36
msgid ""
"Then depend on the coordinates declared in [`java/pom.xml`](https://github."
"com/PRQL/prql/blob/main/prqlc/bindings/java/java/pom.xml) — note that its "
"`<version>` is maintained separately from the PRQL release version, and is "
"not currently bumped on release ([\\#850](https://github.com/PRQL/prql/"
"issues/850)):"
msgstr ""

